00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:41.420
While the broader market navigates these cross currents, one fixed income strategy becomes

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:47.200
especially powerful when rates or inflation are rising. Let us move into today's strategy spotlight

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.540
on floating rate note rotation and rising rate or inflationary regimes. Floating rate notes are

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:58.240
debt instruments whose coupon payments reset periodically. The reset is typically based on a reference

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:04.200
rate like SOFR plus a fixed spread. This built in adjustment mechanism protects investors from

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:10.960
duration risk when interest rates rise or inflation accelerates. Today's combination of oil above $110

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.500
the International Monetary Fund's warning of higher prices and slower growth and persistent

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.500
geopolitical tension makes floating rate notes particularly relevant. Canadian investors holding bonds

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.940
inside tax-free savings accounts or registered retirement savings plans should pay close attention.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.500
Implementation is straightforward on platforms like Questrade or Interactive Brokers.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:38.160
You can screen for investment-grade floating rate notes or simply use exchange-traded funds such as

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:47.020
shares floating rate bond ETF ticker FLOT or the Invesco senior loan ETF ticker BKLN.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.340
Focus on credit quality, reset frequency that is monthly or quarterly and the quoted spread over

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:59.600
the benchmark. Track the effective yield relative to fixed rate alternatives using your broker's fixed

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:06.680
income screener. Historically, this strategy performed well during the 2021-2023 rate hike cycle.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:12.100
Floating rate notes materially outperformed long duration government bonds in that period.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.620
The primary risk remains credit deterioration in the underlying issuers during a sharp economic slowdown.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:24.960
Always size these positions to no more than 10-15% of your fixed income sleeve. Rebalance quarterly

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.800
as spreads compress or widen. With inflation and geopolitical risks front and center,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.240
it is also critical we talk about how liquidity itself behaves during these shock windows.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.680
That brings us to an important lesson on bid-asks, spreads and liquidity fragility in geopolitical

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:45.620
shock windows. Imagine you placed a market order for a mid-cap energy services stock at 935 this

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.940
morning as headlines about Israeli strikes on Beirut and Trump's Iran deadline flashed across

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:59.100
terminals, your order filled at $48.75. Yet when you check the tape, the prevailing bid was $48.10

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:05.900
just 90 seconds later. Market makers widened the bid-asks, spread from a normal 4 cents to 65 cents

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:11.000
within the first 30 minutes of heightened geopolitical news flow. They were protecting themselves

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:17.100
against inventory risk while retail flow rushed in. In today's pre-market environment, with oil

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:24.440
above $110 average spreads on energy and defense-related names expanded three to four times their 20-day average.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:31.340
Algorithms detect volatility spikes, reduce quote-size and widen spreads until order flow balances

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:37.280
or volatility normalizes. A $10,000 round trip trade that normally costs $8.00 in implicit

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:44.600
spread cost can suddenly cost between $65 and $130. Professionals always check the level two tape

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.240
or time and sales window before hitting market orders during news events. They set limit orders

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.040
at or inside the national best bid and offer rather than chasing. Canadian investors using

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:59.020
wealth-simple or quest-raid can enable advanced market data add-ons to see real-time depth.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:04.220
The biggest misconception is believing liquidity is always there when you need it. In reality,

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:10.180
liquidity evaporates precisely when you need it most. Always verify the 20-day average spread

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.800
and current quoted size before trading names expose to geopolitical or commodity shocks.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:20.540
Understanding liquidity risk is essential before we put any capital to work, even simulated capital.

